Copilot / AI Agent Interview Questions
What is the Agent Lifecycle? Explain the different stages involved in designing, developing, testing, deploying, monitoring, and improving an agent.
What is a Multi-Agent System? How does it work, and when would you use multiple agents instead of a single agent?
What is a Multi-Agent Model? How is it different from a traditional single-agent architecture?
What is an Autonomous Agent? How does an autonomous agent make decisions and execute tasks without continuous human intervention?
When we configure a trigger for an agent, is a flow/workflow created behind the scenes? Explain what happens technically when a trigger is configured.
How can we minimize hallucinations in Copilot/AI agents? What techniques can be used to improve the accuracy and reliability of responses?
How would you handle a customer complaint where the AI agent provided an incorrect answer? What troubleshooting, governance, and corrective actions would you take?
What is the difference between a Tool and a Knowledge Source in an AI agent? When should each one be used?
What is a Multi-Model Agent? How can an agent use different AI models for different tasks, and what are the benefits?
How would you create an Autonomous Agent? Explain the key configuration and design considerations.
How would you create an agent that runs automatically every day without specifying an exact execution time? What trigger or scheduling mechanism would you use?
What is RBAC (Role-Based Access Control)? How is RBAC used to control access to agents, tools, data, and environments?
How would you troubleshoot a Copilot agent when its response time is very high?
